## Context

The collection specification (`docs/jetp-collection.md`, accepted in spec
v1, tag `jetp-spec-v1`) fixes the stopping rule and leaves a campaign to
declare, before its first round, what is particular to it. This ticket
writes that declaration for the author to accept. It overlaps M2 (author
decision 2026-10-01, D3); M2 itself targets the register as frozen at 392
documents (369 with a snapshot) and admits nothing new.

What the declaration fixes, by spec section (pointing, not restating):

- § 3, the authority frame: one instance per country (South Africa,
  Indonesia, Viet Nam, Senegal), each expected authority and each project
  listed in an official plan, pipeline or progress list named, so each can
  end with a terminal verdict.
- § 4, the search channel classes per country and language.
- § 5, the stopping rule's tunable numbers for this campaign (starting
  values: 2 %, two quiet rounds in different classes, 90 % known-item
  recall) and the two backstops the spec leaves unset: the **date cap** and
  the **effort cap**.
- § 7, the list of main secondary trackers whose quantitative claims the
  secondary-to-primary pass follows, and the sampling rule if their claims
  exceed the budget.
- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 7.2: the paid web-search budget per campaign
  and the query count per round (proposed USD 25).

The earlier per-country coverage matrices of [[0717]] to [[0720]] are an
input to the frames, not the frames themselves.

Pilot rule (author, 2026-10-01; stated in [[0725]]): the campaign this
protocol governs starts with a pilot round on a stratified sample (country ×
channel class, size stated), quality-checked by a cross-model checker, before
the full campaign; the protocol says so.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An authority-frame instance per country, with every expected authority and listed project named
- [ ] Search channel classes per country and language declared
- [ ] Date cap and effort cap declared; the stopping-rule numbers for this campaign stated (the spec's starting values unless changed)
- [ ] Tracker list declared, with the sampling rule for the secondary-to-primary pass
- [ ] Campaign search budget declared (operation § 7.2), and the pilot round described
- [ ] The author accepts the protocol (collection § 5 "Acceptance"); the acceptance is recorded in [[0725]]
